            <ArticleTitle>Inadvertent injection of sodium hypochlorite into the periradicular tissues during root canal treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-6, 19</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes a sodium hypochlorite (NaOCl) incident occurring during routine endodontic treatment of a patient who presented with chronic periapical periodontitis of a maxillary canine tooth and discusses the immediate and late treatment of this case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
